# The MQL5 sources are stored byte-exactly: no EOL conversion, no renormalising.
#
# `text` would normalise the index to LF and turn the next `git pull` on a
# Windows box with core.autocrlf=true into a whole-file diff - the exact noise
# that hides a real change in a file this size.
#
# The endings are NOT uniform across the tree and no comment here should claim
# they are. As of v6.6.25 it is 11 CRLF files and 36 LF files, with no file
# mixed - but that split is history, not policy, and it has already drifted once
# (this comment used to assert "every QSMC header is LF" while four of them,
# QSMC_Types / QSMC_Root / QSMC_MarketData / QSMC_IncidentSafety, are CRLF).
# What is actually required of anyone editing an MQL5 file here:
#
#   1. preserve the file's existing ending - do not let an editor normalise it;
#   2. check before committing, do not trust a comment:
#        git ls-files '*.mq5' '*.mqh' | while read f; do
#          python3 -c "b=open('$f','rb').read();c=b.count(b'\r\n');print('$f',c,b.count(b'\n')-c)"
#        done
#      a file with both counts non-zero is mixed and must be fixed;
#   3. nadir2.mq5 and MQL5/Indicators/nadir2.mq5 must stay byte-identical, which
#      tools/check_repo_layout.py enforces - edit one, copy to the other.
*.mq5  -text
*.mqh  -text
*.set  -text
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
